# Density Compare
# Copper (Cu) — real density 8.96 g/cm³. equal masses: Copper vs water — sides ∝ (1/ρ)^(1/3).
scene "Copper Density Compare"

element_cube = cube 9.6mm material: copper at (-20mm, 4.8mm, 0)
water_cube = cube 20mm material: water at (18mm, 10mm, 0)
# both cubes weigh the same: about 71.5 g — the water cube is the reference
